      {
        "label": "边框 4 - Border 4",
        "value": "#1E1F22",
        "cssValue": "#1E1F22",
        "description": "Discord's iOS app is a dark-first community UI built around one load-bearing color: Blurple (`#5865F2`). Open the app and you're dropped into a three-pane architecture — a leftmost server rail of rounded-square server icons, a channel list in the middle, and a message thread on the right — compressed into a mobile form factor via horizontal swipe navigation. The canvas is a near-black gradient of grays: the server rail at `#1E1F22`, the channel list at `#2B2D31`, the chat area at `#313338`. These three adjacent grays are so carefully tuned that they read as sibling surfaces rather than competing panels. The whole app feels like a gaming tool: purpose-built, dense, slightly nerdy, unapologetically dark."
      },
      {
        "label": "边框 5 - Border 5",
        "value": "#2B2D31",
        "cssValue": "#2B2D31",
        "description": "Discord's iOS app is a dark-first community UI built around one load-bearing color: Blurple (`#5865F2`). Open the app and you're dropped into a three-pane architecture — a leftmost server rail of rounded-square server icons, a channel list in the middle, and a message thread on the right — compressed into a mobile form factor via horizontal swipe navigation. The canvas is a near-black gradient of grays: the server rail at `#1E1F22`, the channel list at `#2B2D31`, the chat area at `#313338`. These three adjacent grays are so carefully tuned that they read as sibling surfaces rather than competing panels. The whole app feels like a gaming tool: purpose-built, dense, slightly nerdy, unapologetically dark."
